---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Completing the Square Method | Quadratic Equations | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn how to solve quadratic equations by completing the square method with clear steps and solved examples for Class 10 Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/quadratic-equations" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Quadratic Equations</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">03</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 03 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS</div>
					<h1>Completing the <span>Square Method</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master the algebraic technique of transforming quadratic expressions into perfect square forms (x + k)² = d.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · CONCEPT -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · THE METHOD</div>
					<h2>Why Complete the Square?</h2>
					<p>
						Not all quadratic equations are easy to factorise by splitting the middle term. Completing the square converts <em>ax² + bx + c = 0</em> into:
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>(x + b/2a)² = (b² - 4ac) / 4a²</strong>
						<span>This algebraic transformation forms the foundation for deriving the Quadratic Formula!</span>
					</div>

					<div class="idea-box">
						<div class="idea-icon">✓</div>
						<div class="idea-content">
							<strong>The Golden Rule</strong>
							<p>
								To complete the square for <em>x² + px</em>, add and subtract <strong>(p/2)²</strong>, which is square of half the coefficient of x!
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · STEP-BY-STEP PROCEDURE -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · ALGORITHMIC STEPS</div>
					<h2>4 Steps to Complete the Square</h2>

					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Solve 2x² - 5x + 3 = 0 by Completing the Square</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p><strong>Step 1: Divide by 'a' (make coefficient of x² equal to 1)</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								x² - (5/2)x + (3/2) = 0
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:12px;"><strong>Step 2: Move constant term to RHS</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								x² - (5/2)x = -3/2
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:12px;"><strong>Step 3: Add (p/2)² = (-5/4)² = 25/16 to both sides</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								x² - (5/2)x + 25/16 = -3/2 + 25/16<br/>
								(x - 5/4)² = (-24 + 25) / 16<br/>
								<strong>(x - 5/4)² = 1 / 16</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:12px;"><strong>Step 4: Take square root of both sides</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								x - 5/4 = ± 1/4<br/>
								x = 5/4 + 1/4 = 6/4 = <strong>3/2</strong><br/>
								x = 5/4 - 1/4 = 4/4 = <strong>1</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:12px;">Roots are <strong>x = 3/2</strong> and <strong>x = 1</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Always ensure the coefficient of <em>x²</em> is <strong>1</strong> before completing the square.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Add <strong>(p/2)²</strong> (half the coefficient of x squared) to both sides of the equation.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Take square roots on both sides taking care of the <strong>± sign</strong> to obtain both roots.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/quadratic-equations/factorisation" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>Solving by Factorisation</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/quadratic-equations/quadratic-formula" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>The Quadratic Formula</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">QUADRATIC EQUATIONS</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 03 of 05</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
							<div style="width: 60%;"></div>
						</div>

						<div class="sidebar-lessons">
							<a href="/quadratic-equations/introduction" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>01</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Introduction</strong>
									<small>Standard form & basics</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/factorisation" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>02</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Factorisation Method</strong>
									<small>Splitting the middle term</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/completing-the-square" class="sidebar-lesson active">
								<span>03</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Completing the Square</strong>
									<small>Perfect square method</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/quadratic-formula" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>04</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Quadratic Formula</strong>
									<small>Formula & solutions</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/nature-of-roots" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>05</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Nature of Roots</strong>
									<small>Discriminant D = b² - 4ac</small>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
